    fix(cli): add --version flag so the remote update check works (CLI-VERSION-001)
    
    `duckbrain --version` did not exist, so the remote update check
    (src/ssh/client.ts checkRemoteInstall) always saw versionResult.status !== 0
    on its second SSH call and returned {installed:true, needsUpdate:false} —
    silently reporting "up to date" forever. client.test.ts mocks the missing
    command, so the defect stayed green.
    
    - bin/duckbrain.ts: print `duckbrain v<version>` and exit 0 for --version /
      -v anywhere in the args. The version is read from package.json at runtime
      via __dirname (the package is CommonJS; bin/ sits beside package.json).
      The check runs before socket routing, so `--socket=<name> --version`
      cannot be swallowed by runRemoteCLI.
    - showHelp(): document `--version, -v`.
    - src/cli/version-cli001.test.ts: spawn-based regression tests driving the
      real bin/duckbrain.js entry (--version, -v, --socket=<name> --version,
      and help lists --version), asserting the /(\d+\.\d+\.\d+)/ contract the
      SSH parser consumes. RED-proven against the pre-fix blob (4/4 fail).
    
    src/ssh/client.ts is unchanged — the existing path starts working once the
    command exists. The existing parsing test in client.test.ts already covers
    `duckbrain v1.0.0` -> "1.0.0".
    
